<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115084617 +0000" stop="20261115090834 +0000">
    <title>Bright Now S1 - "The Science of Cute"</title>
    <desc>Domestication shaped wolves into dogs and transformed both their behavior and their anatomy. New discoveries show how dogs produce a very specific eyebrow movement more often than wolves do.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115090834 +0000" stop="20261115094657 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 1"</title>
    <desc>The rains have arrived, and the desert has never looked better. Cleo, the boss of this group of wild meerkats has given birth to five new pups, but some of them quickly get lost or snatched away. Only the toughest survive here in the African desert.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115094657 +0000" stop="20261115102520 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 2"</title>
    <desc>In another cruel twist, Cleo’s young pup Ophelia got left behind on a foraging trip and was killed by one of the Kalahari’s most dangerous creatures, a Goshawk. The remaining three pups: Zeus, Daisy and Flo struggle to survive.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115102520 +0000" stop="20261115110343 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 3"</title>
    <desc>The Gosa Gang have recently moved to a new home, close to the Gosa Dam where a rival family of meerkats live. In the quest for territorial dominance, a major meerkat standoff resulted in both gangs losing a member of their tribe.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115110343 +0000" stop="20261115114206 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 4"</title>
    <desc>Recently Priscilla bought an adopted boy pup from a rival gang to the Gosa Burrow. Unfortunately, his acceptance into the Gosa group was far from ideal. The rest of the gang went out and he was left alone at the burrow, struggling for his life.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115114206 +0000" stop="20261115122028 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 5"</title>
    <desc>Summer has arrived. The Gang move to an area known as the Whispering Forest as it is the best place to find food at this time of year. However, the grass is long and there are several predators lurking such as a leopard.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115122028 +0000" stop="20261115125851 +0000">
    <title>Kalahari Meerkats S2 - "Episode 6"</title>
    <desc>The Gosa Gang are on their way home from the Whispering Forest and bump head on into their bitter enemies. To get past them and move over the mountain a full-on war breaks out.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115125851 +0000" stop="20261115132830 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "Responsible Fishing"</title>
    <desc>In this episode we look at the WWF Responsible Fisheries Programme. Dr. Samantha Petersen, the programme manager, tells exactly us what this entails and Tali dons her waterproofs and sets sail where she chats to fishermen and others in the industry.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115132830 +0000" stop="20261115135811 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "West Coast Marine Protected Area"</title>
    <desc>In this episode we show just how valuable this marine protected area is.Tali meets up with a group of scientists who are doing various studies so that they can assess the fish stocks and look at what role the mpa has in managing these stocks.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115135811 +0000" stop="20261115142738 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "De Hoop Marine Protected Area"</title>
    <desc>In this episode Tali explores the various creatures that reside in De Hoop Marine Protected Area, from the Greater White Pelicans and Chacma baboons to the large Eland.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115142738 +0000" stop="20261115145720 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "Cape Agulhas"</title>
    <desc>Cape Agulhas is the true meeting place of the Atlantic and Indian Oceans, a place of immense cultural and natural value. Tali searches for answers to her burning questions about establishing new parks and the roles communities play in this process.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115145720 +0000" stop="20261115152702 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "Cedarberg Biodiversity"</title>
    <desc>Using a novel conservation model, the Greater Cedarberg Biodiversity Initiative is ensuring that the land is used in an efficient way, with the land and its inhabitants work in harmony. Tali investigate the various ways being used to achieve this.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115152702 +0000" stop="20261115155631 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "Cape Floristic Region"</title>
    <desc>Tali investigates the struggle to protect the Cape Floristic Region, one of the world’s 6 floral kingdoms and the only one entirely within the borders of a single country. She finds out more about why this region is in critical need of conservation.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115155631 +0000" stop="20261115162614 +0000">
    <title>Keepers Of The Cape - The Issues S1 - "Working For Water"</title>
    <desc>In this episode we turn our attention to the damaging effects of invasive alien plants on our country’s water supply. Tali looks at three initiatives, Working for Wetlands; Working for Water and the Water Neutral Scheme.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115162614 +0000" stop="20261115165557 +0000">
    <title>City Zoo S1 - "Big Cats"</title>
    <desc>In this episode we meet the Big Cats. The zoo crew treats a tiger called Lolo with a toothache. Adrian and Jacquie rescue three teenage lion cubs from an illegal facility and transport them to their new home at City Zoo.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115165557 +0000" stop="20261115172539 +0000">
    <title>City Zoo S1 - "Rhino’s"</title>
    <desc>In this episode we learn to tell the difference between both the white and black rhino residents. Adrian and the zoo crew travel to the Lichtenburg Breeding centre to monitor a herd of white rhino.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115172539 +0000" stop="20261115175522 +0000">
    <title>City Zoo S1 - "The Birds"</title>
    <desc>In this episode Cape Vultures are given a new lease on life. The zoo crew monitors the success of their Cape Vulture breeding program, so that this rare species endures.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115175522 +0000" stop="20261115182505 +0000">
    <title>City Zoo S1 - "Primates"</title>
    <desc>In this episode Adrian, the zoo vet, treats Lesser White monkey with a weight issue. The zoo's three chimpanzees have their annual health check and Adrian becomes concerned that the eldest female is showing signs of ill health.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261115182505 +0000" stop="20261115192333 +0000">
    <title>Green China Rising</title>
    <desc>From the world’s biggest polluter to a powerhouse of green innovation, China’s fight for survival begins now.</desc>
